The vertex of the parabola is $(2, -\frac{1}{2})$. Therefore, the graphs of $y = f(x)$ and $y = g(x)$ intersect at one point, so $a = 1$.

The graph of the quadratic function is also symmetric about the line $x = -2$. The graphs of $y = f(x)$ and $y = h(x)$ intersect at the point where the two graphs are equal, which is on the line of symmetry. Therefore, the graphs of $y = f(x)$ and $y = h(x)$ intersect at two points, one leading to $a$ and one leading to $b$. Thus, $b = 2$.

Therefore, $10a + b = 10(1) + 2 = \boxed{12}$.

